# A widget defined inside a widget block, `@line:` and its block, in the same form as at
# the top of a file (Semantics ch. 3: `fn` "defines a function in the block, in the same
# form as at the top of a file", and a widget definition is the `@` form of one; ch. 4: a
# widget block's names are one binding group). It reads the block's `n` and is built by
# each bare `@line`. Written by Claude on the claude-lowering branch; subject to change.
emit Ui.*
test mod Tests
use Ui.*

@page: @unit
@page:
    let n = 7
    @line:
        Ui.Label($text=$"line {n}")
    @line                                                        # 0
    @line                                                        # 1
    Ui.Label($text=$"end")                                       # 2
